// Compute once — not inside the update loop
const SUM_OF_RADII = BALL_RADIUS + PIN_COLLISION_RADIUS;

// Level-triggered: fires every frame the condition is true
const dist = ballMesh.position.distanceTo(pinMesh.position);
if (dist < SUM_OF_RADII) { /* may run 30+ times for one collision */ }

// Edge-triggered: fires at most once per pin per throw
const hitPins = new Set();
// ...
if (dist < SUM_OF_RADII && !hitPins.has(pin)) {
  hitPins.add(pin);  // mark processed — block will not run again
  // first-contact response here
}
hitPins.clear(); // reset at end of throw
``` Tunnelling at High Speeds The sphere-sphere test only checks overlap at the current frame position. If the ball moves more than `SUM_OF_RADII` in one frame it can pass completely through a pin without detection — this is called tunnelling. At 5 m/s and 60 fps the ball moves about 0.083 m per frame, well within the 0.18 m detection zone. At very high speeds a swept-sphere (capsule) test is required. Sphere Collision: Detection and Response All cells use Three.js 3D mode. OrbitControls active. assignment homework quiz exam practice problems worked example step by step

